+# Feature Specification: Create JSON Patch
+
+**Input**: Export `createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`; returns an RFC 6902 patch that turns `from` into `to`.
+
+## Requirements
+- `applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to))` deep-equals `to`; equal documents give `[]`.
+- The patch is minimal in spirit: only the changed parts are described, never the whole document
+  when a small place differs. Objects are diffed per member, recursively.
+- Arrays: common leading/trailing elements are skipped; the middle is diffed element by element,
+  then surplus elements are removed (highest index first) or appended with `add`.
+- Differing types (or primitives) at a location produce `replace` (at the root, path `""`).
+- Pointer tokens are escaped (`~0`, `~1`); `__proto__` members are plain data.
+- Inputs are never mutated and the patch shares no structure with them.
+
+## Verification
+`test/createpatch.test.ts` checks round-trips, minimality, escaping, and non-mutation.
